 # Lighting, Shadowing & Relighting
 
-Also called: 3DGS Lighting, Gaussian Splatting Shading, Deferred Gaussian Rendering, T_light Self-Shadowing
+Also called: Deferred Surfel Rendering, Split-Sum IBL
 
 ## Overview
-This family extends 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) rendering to support dynamic, physically-based lighting and self-occlusion. Standard 3DGS bakes lighting into spherical harmonics (SH) or uses fixed forward shading, preventing real-time environment changes or accurate shadows [3459-analytic-splatting-forward-shading.md]. These methods solve that by either deferring material attributes to a G-buffer for split-sum environment map integration [4464-ref-gaussian-deferred-surfel-rendering-with-split-sum-ibl.md] or by performing a dedicated light-space rasterization pass to compute front-facing transmittance for self-shadowing [4487-3d-gaussian-splatting-self-shadowing-t_light.md, 4489-light-space-rasterization-for-t_light.md].
+This family extends 3D Gaussian Splatting to support physically based lighting, self-occlusion, and environment reflections. It solves the limitation of standard splatting, which assumes a fixed, uniform lighting environment, by introducing deferred shading pipelines for relighting [4464-ref-gaussian-deferred-surfel-rendering-with-split-sum-ibl.md] and dedicated light-space rasterization passes for self-shadowing [4487-3d-gaussian-splatting-self-shadowing-t_light.md, 4489-light-space-rasterization-for-t_light.md]. Unlike sibling methods that may use simplified shading functions or voxel-based fallbacks, these approaches provide full PBR material attributes and continuous differentiable gradients for shadows without modifying the primary camera's covariance expansion [4464-ref-gaussian-deferred-surfel-rendering-with-split-sum-ibl.md, 4487-3d-gaussian-splatting-self-shadowing-t_light.md, 4489-light-space-rasterization-for-t_light.md].
 
